findings.claim:
The class 'spellings that reach RescanAsAdministrator.Start without spelling RescanAsAdministrator.Start' is still open through the project-file spelling of a global using. Directory.Build.props:5 sets <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>. So <Using Include="FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator" Static="true" /> (or Alias="RA") in src/FsAnalyser.App/FsAnalyser.App.csproj, a src Directory.Build.*, or the root Directory.Build.props/targets generates `global using static global::FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator;` into obj/.../FsAnalyser.App.GlobalUsings.g.cs. After that, a bare `Start(Environment.ProcessPath, root, Process.Start)` compiles in every App file, MainWindow.xaml.cs's OnLoaded included. Nothing catches it:
- the call-site entry's files are src/**/*.cs, so it never reads a project file;
- its patterns do not match a <Using> item;
- Fitness reads git-visible files, not obj (332 files read, while src/**/obj alone holds 32 .cs files), and RescanElevationRulesCorpusTests.FilesOf drops bin and obj;
- RescanElevationGuardTests checks directives only in MainWindow.xaml.cs's own text, and its Start counters only see the qualified spelling.
The corpus note bounds the class by 'whoever edits src, a project file or the window hook next', so a project-file spelling is inside the bound the build claimed closed. Measured: the repro below fails 3 of 3 on this tree, with 'no SL-008 entry reads ... and fires on: <Using Include=...>'.

repro.body:
using System.Text.RegularExpressions;

namespace FsAnalyser.Core.Tests;

// Code review of SL-008, attempt 2: with ImplicitUsings on (Directory.Build.props), a <Using> item in a project file or a root
// build file becomes a 'global using static global::FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator;' (or an alias) in the generated
// GlobalUsings.g.cs under obj, which no rule reads. A bare Start(...) in any App file then reaches the elevation. Some settled
// SL-008 entry has to read those files and fire on that item, whatever entry it is.
public class CrSl008ProjectFileUsingTests
{
    private static string[] Sl008RuleNames()
    {
        string[] lines = File.ReadAllLines(Path.Combine(FailCriticalErrorsTests.FindRepo(), ".taad", "fitness.yaml"));
        int start = Array.FindIndex(lines, l => l.Trim() == "# settled by SL-008");
        Assert.True(start >= 0, "no '# settled by SL-008' block in .taad/fitness.yaml");
        var names = new List<string>();
        for (int i = start + 1; i < lines.Length; i++)
        {
            string t = lines[i].Trim();
            if (t.StartsWith("# settled by", StringComparison.Ordinal))
                break;
            if (t.StartsWith("- name: ", StringComparison.Ordinal))
            {
                string n = t["- name: ".Length..].Trim();
                names.Add(n.Length >= 2 && n[0] == '\'' && n[^1] == '\'' ? n[1..^1].Replace("''", "'") : n);
            }
        }
        return [.. names];
    }

    private static bool GlobMatches(string glob, string path)
    {
        string re = Regex.Escape(glob).Replace(@"\*\*/", "(.*/)?").Replace(@"\*\*", ".*").Replace(@"\*", "[^/]*");
        return Regex.IsMatch(path, "^" + re + "$", RegexOptions.IgnoreCase);
    }

    [Theory]
    [InlineData("src/FsAnalyser.App/FsAnalyser.App.csproj", "    <Using Include=\"FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator\" Static=\"true\" />")]
    [InlineData("src/FsAnalyser.App/FsAnalyser.App.csproj", "    <Using Include=\"FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator\" Alias=\"RA\" />")]
    [InlineData("Directory.Build.props", "    <Using Include=\"FsAnalyser.App.RescanAsAdministrator\" Static=\"true\" />")]
    public void AProjectFileUsingOfTheRescanClassIsCaughtBySomeSettledEntry(string file, string line)
    {
        bool caught = Sl008RuleNames()
            .Select(SettledRulesCorpusTests.ReadRule)
            .Any(rule => GlobMatches(rule.Files, file)
                && !rule.ExceptFiles.Contains(file, StringComparer.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                && rule.Patterns.Any(p => Regex.IsMatch(line, p)));
        Assert.True(caught, $"no SL-008 entry reads {file} and fires on: {line.Trim()}");
    }
}
